{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe drive to Saint-Denis and Montmorency was pleasant, though the cathedral’s black drapery for a funeral gave the morning a solemn air. I rode a donkey to the Hermitage, Rousseau’s old retreat, and we climbed the heights. From there, the view of Paris and Montmartre was magnificent. It is strange to see the city from such a distance, reduced to a patchwork of roofs and smoke.\n\nI thought of how we often chase grandeur in the public square, when the true perspective comes only from a quiet elevation. The day was warm, and the air fresh. I feel rested, though my legs ache from the climb. Please tell the boys that Father is well and has seen the very spot where the *Social Contract* was born, if only in the ruins of a garden.\n\nI miss you and the comfort of our Berlin home. Write soon.\n\nYour loving,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080588,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":203,"prompt_tokens":952,"total_tokens":1155,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-XZdUgyUSrB5CCM6jCakhqw0plIgfNuiV","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":952,"prompt_ms":929.25,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9761029411764706,"prompt_per_second":1024.482109227872,"predicted_n":203,"predicted_ms":4845.026,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.985277227722772,"predicted_per_second":41.692242724806846}}